Notebook[{
Cell["A Locally Invertible Hypergraph Rule as a Toy Model of Information Loss in Conformal Cyclic Cosmology", "Title"],
Cell["Edwin Rosero (independent researcher) \[CenterDot] Companion notebook to the Wolfram Community follow-up post \[CenterDot] github.com/walkthroughwonder/discrete-jacobian \[CenterDot] doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21630926", "Subtitle"],
Cell["This notebook reproduces every result in the post from scratch: the flagship splice collision, the loop-count termination property, and the exhaustive information-loss measurement. Evaluate the cells in order (Evaluation \[FilledSmallTriangle] Evaluate Notebook). Total runtime for E \[LessEqual] 5 is well under a minute.", "Text"],
Cell["1. Definitions", "Section"],
Cell["The rule is {{a,a},{b,c}} \[Rule] {{a,b},{c,a}}. States are binary-edge hypergraphs (self-loops and multi-edges allowed), compared up to isomorphism via a canonical form that permutes vertices within classes of equal (out-degree, in-degree, loop count).", "Text"],
Cell["(* Canonical form: brute force over permutations within vertex classes of
   equal (out-degree, in-degree, loop count). Valid canonical form. *)
spliceCanon[st_List] := Module[{vs, sig, cls, perms, cands},
  If[st === {}, Return[{}]];
  vs = Union @@ st;
  sig = Association[# -> {Count[st, {#, x_} /; x =!= #],
        Count[st, {x_, #} /; x =!= #], Count[st, {#, #}]} & /@ vs];
  cls = GatherBy[SortBy[vs, sig], sig];
  perms = Tuples[Permutations /@ cls];
  cands = Table[With[{m = AssociationThread[Flatten[p], Range[0, Length[vs] - 1]]},
      Sort[st /. m]], {p, perms}];
  First[Sort[cands]]];

spliceRelabel[st_] := With[{m = AssociationThread[Union @@ st,
      Range[0, Length[Union @@ st] - 1]]}, Sort[st /. m]];

(* All one-step successors, as canonical forms (all matches, no policy) *)
spliceSuccessors[st_] := Union@Flatten[Table[
     If[st[[i, 1]] == st[[i, 2]] && j != i && Length[Union[{st[[i, 1]]}, st[[j]]]] == 3,
      {spliceCanon@spliceRelabel@Join[Delete[st, {{i}, {j}}],
          {{st[[i, 1]], st[[j, 1]]}, {st[[j, 2]], st[[i, 1]]}}]}, {}],
     {i, Length[st]}, {j, Length[st]}], 2];

(* Every state (binary edges, loops and multi-edges allowed) with 0..maxE edges *)
spliceStateLayers[maxE_] := NestList[Function[prev, Union@Flatten[Table[
       With[{n = Length[Union @@ Append[s, {}]]},
        Table[spliceCanon@spliceRelabel@Append[s, {x, y}], {x, 0, n + 1}, {y, 0, n + 1}]],
       {s, prev}], 2]], {{}}, maxE];

(* Deterministic evolution: min-successor policy, run until no match remains *)
spliceEndpoint[s_] := NestWhile[First@Sort@spliceSuccessors[#] &, s,
   spliceSuccessors[#] =!= {} &];

entropyBits[c_] := With[{p = N[c/Total[c]]}, -Total[p Log2[p]]];

(* Bits of the initial state not recoverable from the terminal state,
   per (E, V) sector, over all states with at least one loop *)
spliceInformationLoss[maxE_] := Module[{layers = spliceStateLayers[maxE]},
  Flatten[Table[
    With[{act = Select[layers[[e + 1]],
         Count[#, {a_, a_}] > 0 && Length[Union @@ #] == v &]},
     If[act === {}, Nothing,
      With[{f = Values@Counts[spliceEndpoint /@ act]},
       <|\"E\" -> e, \"V\" -> v, \"StatesWithLoop\" -> Length[act],
        \"Endpoints\" -> Length[f], \"MaxFiber\" -> Max[f],
        \"BitsLost\" -> Round[Log2[N@Length[act]] - entropyBits[f], 0.001]|>]]],
    {e, 1, maxE}, {v, 1, 2 e}], 1]];

loopCount[s_] := Count[s, {a_, a_}];", "Input"],
Cell["2. The flagship collision", "Section"],
Cell["Two non-isomorphic, mutually unreachable states evolve to the same state. Each has a single successor class.", "Text"],
Cell["s1 = spliceCanon[{{0, 0}, {1, 2}, {1, 3}}];  (* loop + out-star *)
s2 = spliceCanon[{{0, 0}, {1, 2}, {3, 2}}];  (* loop + in-star *)
<|\"NonIsomorphic\" -> (s1 =!= s2),
  \"Successors1\" -> spliceSuccessors[s1],
  \"Successors2\" -> spliceSuccessors[s2],
  \"SameImage\" -> (spliceSuccessors[s1] === spliceSuccessors[s2])|>", "Input"],
Cell["g[st_, lbl_, opts___] := Graph[DirectedEdge @@@ st, opts, VertexStyle -> Black,
   EdgeStyle -> Directive[Darker@Blue, Thick], PlotLabel -> Style[lbl, 13],
   ImageSize -> {190, 150}, VertexSize -> 0.1];
arrow[s_] := Graphics[Text[Style[s, 26, Gray]], ImageSize -> {50, 150}];
GraphicsRow[{g[{{0, 0}, {1, 2}, {1, 3}}, \"S1: loop + out-star\"], arrow[\"\\[LongRightArrow]\"],
  g[{{1, 2}, {2, 3}, {3, 0}}, \"shared image: directed 4-path\",
   VertexCoordinates -> {1 -> {0, 0}, 2 -> {1, 0}, 3 -> {2, 0}, 0 -> {3, 0}}],
  arrow[\"\\[LongLeftArrow]\"], g[{{0, 0}, {1, 2}, {3, 2}}, \"S2: loop + in-star\"]},
 ImageSize -> 780, Spacings -> 0]", "Input"],
Cell["3. Termination: the loop count is a clock", "Section"],
Cell["Every application consumes exactly one loop and creates none, so an evolution from a state with L loops halts within at most L steps. The first check confirms this over every state with up to 5 edges. The second counts how many evolutions run all the way to a loop-free state (expected: 15/28, 126/166, 914/1036).", "Text"],
Cell["layers = spliceStateLayers[5];
AllTrue[Flatten[layers, 1], Function[s,
  AllTrue[spliceSuccessors[s], loopCount[#] == loopCount[s] - 1 &]]]", "Input"],
Cell["Table[With[{act = Select[layers[[e + 1]], loopCount[#] > 0 &]},
  <|\"E\" -> e, \"EndsLoopFree\" -> Count[spliceEndpoint /@ act, s_ /; loopCount[s] == 0],
   \"StatesWithLoop\" -> Length[act]|>], {e, 3, 5}] // Dataset", "Input"],
Cell["4. Information loss", "Section"],
Cell["For each (E, V) sector: bits lost = log2(#states with a loop) \[Minus] H(terminal state), using the min-successor policy. Change 5 to 6 to reproduce the E = 6 row (a few minutes).", "Text"],
Cell["data = spliceInformationLoss[5];
Dataset[data]", "Input"],
Cell["peak = MaximalBy[#, #BitsLost &][[1]] & /@ GroupBy[data, #E &];
Dataset[Values[peak]]", "Input"],
Cell["ListLinePlot[KeyValueMap[{#1, #2[\"BitsLost\"]} &, peak] // Select[#[[1]] >= 3 &],
 Mesh -> All, MeshStyle -> PointSize[Large], Frame -> True,
 FrameLabel -> {\"edges E\", \"bits of initial state lost\"},
 PlotLabel -> \"Information lost by the terminal state (peak sector)\",
 PlotRange -> {0, Automatic}, GridLines -> {None, Automatic}, ImageSize -> 520]", "Input"],
Cell["5. Notes", "Section"],
Cell["Results agree exactly with an independent Python implementation in the repository (phase1/ccc_compression.py, phase1/ccc_policy_fmin.py), which extends the sweep to E = 6. This is a structural analogy with conformal cyclic cosmology, not a cosmological claim; see the post for limitations and open questions. Prepared with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic), disclosed.", "Text"]
}, WindowSize -> {900, 800}, StyleDefinitions -> "Default.nb"]
